and stylized icons against a dark blue to bright cyan gradient background. At the top, a stylized banner with the title. Below it, a clean diagram shows the system architecture in four main components, connected by flow lines. On the left, a vertical pane\
l 'MOBILE CLIENT LAYER \(Guard App\)' with sub-icons: GPS Geofence \(20m-50m, location icon\), Anti-Spoofing \(glowing shield with camera\), Live Selfie \(biometric camera icon\), and Offline-First \(disconnected cloud icon with arrows\). Connected to it \
is a center component 'BACKEND & SERVICES \(API Gateway\)', with 'DATA FLOW' and 'SECURITY \(JWT, HTTPS\)' labels. Below this center component is 'DATABASE LAYER', showcasing PostGIS \(geospatial icon\) and PostgreSQL. To the right of the central hub is a\
 large 'ADMIN & MONITORING LAYER' component \(desktop monitor and tablet\), with 'Web Admin Portal' and sub-panels: Real-time Live Map \(guard pins on a map\), Flagged Exceptions \(red 'flagged' icon\), Alert Dispatch \(Telegram/WhatsApp icons\), and HRIS\
 Integration \(REST API icon with gears\). A horizontal process arrow flow 'PHASED DEPLOYMENT TIMELINE' spans the lower middle: Phase 1 \(1-2 Weeks\) -> Phase 2 \(3-5 Weeks\) -> Phase 3 \(5-7 Weeks\) -> Phase 4 \(8-9 Weeks\) -> Phase 5 \(10 Weeks\). Each \
point has tiny step labels. On the far right, a vertical summary column 'KEY SYSTEM BENEFITS': Accurate Geospatial Verification, proxy attendance elimination, automated incident alerting, and fault-tolerant operations. The overall style is clean, modern, \
